
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Four weeks ago I was in downtown Manhattan for the world premiere event for&nbsp;<a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lI7tMxzSJ7w"><em>C++: The Documentary</em></a>. It was great to see two theaters full of enthusiastic C++ developers, and getting to mingle with them all before and after the film.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Afterwards we had a live panel: Bjarne Stroustrup, Gabriel Dos Reis, Nina Ranns, Eric Lubin, and me; Matt Godbolt (yes, <em>the</em> Matt Godbolt) was our moderator. <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zMYZ5MFQAho"><strong>The video is now on YouTube.</strong></a> I think this is one of the best panels I&#8217;ve ever participated in, thanks to Matt&#8217;s great questions and direction, and the concise and insightful comments from all the panelists. I think each of us only gave one (or maybe two) three-minute answers&#8230; the others were all under two minutes which kept things moving very nicely.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Thanks again to Matt, the panelists, everyone in the crowd of folks who came to see the documentary, and CultRepo and HRT who made the documentary! And thanks most of all to Bjarne Stroustrup, who is the reason we&#8217;re all here and writing high-level high-performance code, portably across all platforms large and small, at a scale and a level of safe abstraction (that continues to improve release after release) we couldn&#8217;t do with just C.</p>



